'' The CVx / MKx family: a number's BYTES as a string and back. Every width has its own
'' entry point, and the pair is NOT symmetric -- there is no fb_CVI at all, so 'cvi'
'' follows the INTEGER width and is fb_CVLONGINT on win64 and fb_CVL on win32, while
'' fb_MKI does exist and takes int64 there and int32 here. Both measured on both
'' targets; neither is guessable from the other half of the family.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/cv-mk.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl i64 fb_CVLONGINT
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_MKI
'' GOLDEN: expected/cv-mk.out
